From: Stereolabs <embedded@stereolabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tegra: snapshot task comm with get_task_comm() in syncpt alloc

tegra_drm_ioctl_syncpoint_allocate() passes current->comm directly as
the syncpoint name. A concurrent set_task_comm() (e.g. the h264 encoder
startup thread being renamed) is a torn read of the comm[] array; the
syncpoint-naming consistency check can WARN(), whose serial-console
write stalls the CPU long enough that the host1x IVC worker is not
scheduled within 50ms, tripping nvargus' 'Status syncpoint signaled but
status value not updated' watchdog and stopping all streams.
get_task_comm() takes task->alloc_lock and strscpy()'s a stable copy.
Ported to R36.5 (unchanged NVIDIA baseline vs R36.4).
---
diff --git a/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/uapi.c b/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/uapi.c
index 0f9342b..9ecee6d 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/uapi.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/uapi.c
@@ -315,11 +315,13 @@ int tegra_drm_ioctl_syncpoint_allocate(struct drm_device *drm, void *data, struc
 	struct drm_tegra_syncpoint_allocate *args = data;
 	struct host1x_syncpt *sp;
 	int err;
+	char comm[TASK_COMM_LEN];
 
 	if (args->id)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	sp = host1x_syncpt_alloc(host1x, HOST1X_SYNCPT_CLIENT_MANAGED, current->comm);
+	get_task_comm(comm, current);
+	sp = host1x_syncpt_alloc(host1x, HOST1X_SYNCPT_CLIENT_MANAGED, comm);
 	if (!sp)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
